Commits on top of upstream eggnog-mapper main @ 6ab05b3
("docs: add beta warning to README")

=== f4dc9f7 feat: merge Foldseek structural search modes onto v3

Ports the eggnog-mapper-foldseek fork (gbouras13, based on v2.1.13) onto
v3.0.0-beta2. The fork had no common history with this repo, so its
snapshot is grafted onto the v2.1.13 commit (8abf461) as a second parent
to give future merges a real merge base.

New:
- eggnogmapper/search/foldseek/: ModernProst 3Di inference (inference.py,
  profiles.py), Foldseek DB creation (create_fs_db.py), the searcher
  (foldseek.py) and the no-hit FASTA helpers (filter.py).
- Search modes foldseek, diamond-foldseek, mmseqs-foldseek.
- --gpu for the MMseqs2/Foldseek GPU prefilter.

Adapted to v3 rather than copied:
- Tools resolve through shutil.which + require_tool(); no LOCAL_* paths,
  since v3 dropped the vendored eggnogmapper/bin/ binaries.
- output_seeds() lost its outfmt_short argument.
- run_generator() keeps its (n, total_time) contract; the annotated query
  ids are collected through a new collect_ids set instead. The fork's
  key_fn=lambda x: x[0] scooped whole hit rows into the set, since items
  are (hit, annotation) pairs.
- Emapper.run() (renamed from run_full_pipeline) drives the second stage,
  and annotate() now returns (annotated_hits, _resumed_ref).
- The Foldseek stage output files are registered in _output_files, so
  --override/--resume and the scratch-dir copy handle them.
- The second stage no longer passes the predictor to search(), which
  would have discarded the filtered FASTA, and no longer renames the
  gene-prediction outputs that wrap_up() moves.
- The two-stage modes now require --itype proteins/CDS: they diff query
  names against the input FASTA, which gene prediction invalidates.
- FoldseekSearcher is imported lazily so torch/transformers stay an
  optional extra rather than a hard dependency of every run.
- .gitignore: '*old*' matched "f-old-seek" and ignored the whole package.

Not carried over: the fork's vendored binaries (v3 removed them),
container/setonix/Dockerfile (site-specific, installs from the fork with
a token) — Foldseek was added to apptainer/eggnog-mapper.def instead.

=== d2b9b88 feat(foldseek): 12-state alphabet support, switch to modernprost-50M-pssm

Adapts the Foldseek integration to the Foldseek build in
fs-dev/foldseek_retry_newref, which adds a 12-state structural alphabet
next to 3Di, and switches 3Di/12st prediction to
gbouras13/modernprost-50M-pssm.

Model:
- ModernProst3Di12StModel returns logits as a dict
  {"3di": (B,L,20), "12st": (B,L,12)}, so one forward pass yields both
  alphabets. split_logits() handles that and still accepts a plain
  tensor (3Di only) from single-head checkpoints.
- One checkpoint now serves both the discrete and the --profiles paths,
  replacing modernprost-base and modernprost-profiles. Their hardcoded
  HF blob MD5 tables are gone; check_model_download() just verifies a
  usable snapshot is cached and lets huggingface_hub do integrity.
- inference.py writes input_12st.fasta beside input_3di.fasta and
  returns both paths.

Database encoding:
- Foldseek packs both alphabets into one byte per residue,
  3Di_state * 12 + 12st_state, and flags _ss with
  DBTYPE_EXTENDED_3DI_12ST (32) in the high half of the dbtype
  (_ss.dbtype reads [0,0,32,0]). Alphabet orders are those of
  data/mat3di.out (ACDEFGHIKLMNPQRSTVWY, X=20 for masked) and
  data/mat12st.out (ACDEFGHIKLMN, no X).
- `foldseek tsv2db` cannot produce this: the packed bytes span 0..251 and
  would collide with TAB/NUL/newline in a TSV, and --output-dbtype cannot
  set the extended bit. write_packed_ss_db() writes the data/index/dbtype
  files directly instead, entries as <bytes> + '\n' + '\0'.
- Verified byte-for-byte against an _ss database Foldseek itself built
  from PDB structures, and end to end with the real model and binary:
  6 globins from sequence each recover their own structure as top hit,
  with self-hit bitscores ~30% above 3Di alone (726 -> 964 etc.).

Search:
- --ss_12st (default 1) maps to Foldseek's --ss-12st, which the search
  workflow forwards to --aux-score, covering prefilter and alignment.
- A packed query against a target DB without the 12 states is not an
  error: Foldseek falls back to 3Di-only scoring and returns exactly the
  --ss_12st 0 results. That would make the flag look effective while
  changing nothing, so db_has_12st() inspects <target>_ss.dbtype and
  warns, pointing at `foldseek add12st`.
- --profiles writes _ss as an MMseqs PSSM db (dbtype 2), which has no
  room for the packed byte, so it forces --ss_12st 0.

Also fixes an f-string with nested double quotes in the --profiles path,
which was a SyntaxError on the Python 3.9-3.11 that setup.cfg allows.

=== ab4664a docs: add conda environment spec for the Foldseek/ModernProst stack

environment-foldseek.yml builds an environment that can run the Foldseek
search modes end to end, inference included: eggnog-mapper's core deps,
the search backends (diamond, mmseqs2, hmmer, prodigal - all have
linux-aarch64 builds), cython for the annotator extensions, and
torch/transformers via pip.

torch is left to pip because the wheel index depends on platform and
CUDA version; the file defaults to the CUDA 13 index and documents the
cu128/cpu alternatives. Verified on aarch64 + NVIDIA GB10 (sm_121) with
torch 2.13.0+cu130, transformers 5.14.1, python 3.12.

foldseek is deliberately not a dependency: bioconda's build has no
--ss-12st, so a 12-state-capable build has to be put on PATH separately
(or --ss_12st 0 used). Noted in the file and in USAGE.md.

=== e5dbfb9 feat: allow annotation against a converted eggNOG v5 database

The v7 database v3 requires is not published (downloads.eggnogdb.org
carries only emapperdb-5.0.2, and no version has the manifest.json the
downloader now demands). This makes a v5 set usable for annotation.

scripts/v5_to_v7_db.py rewrites a v5 eggnog.db into the v7 core schema:
  og            -> ogs        (name kept as "cluster@taxid")
  event         -> sp_events  (CSV-of-names sides -> delta-varint id BLOBs)
  prots.name    -> protein_names + integer-keyed prots
  prots.orthoindex -> event_index
  ref_terms is created empty (get_ref_term has no callers).

Two v7 columns have no v5 source. sp_overlap is computed faithfully as the
species-set Jaccard of the two sides. ev_lca is computed as the deepest
common ancestor of the event's species via LineageCache when --taxa-db is
given, else falls back to the v5 event level. Note taxa.db stores `track`
leaf->root, contrary to LineageCache.tracks()' docstring.

Two code changes were needed for v5-derived data:

- Seed IDs: v7 target DBs name sequences by integer protein ID, v5 ones by
  "TAXID.PROTEIN". batch_annotate now resolves a non-integer seed through
  protein_names (new AnnotDB.get_protein_id, the inverse of the existing
  get_protein_name) instead of dropping it. The drop reason for a seed that
  resolves neither way is renamed non_integer_seed_id ->
  unresolvable_seed_id.

- OG names: _parse_ogs_string required the v7 "cluster@taxid|clade" form and
  silently skipped v5's "cluster@taxid", leaving eggNOG_OGs, max_annot_lvl,
  COG_category and Description empty. It now accepts both. v7 parsing is
  unchanged (verified against 1-, 2- and 3-part names).

Verified end to end on the v5 fixture DB: 2/2 queries annotated, 0 dropped,
14-17 of 25 columns populated, and the calls are correct - ychF/COG0012
GTPase with MMR_HSR1+YchF-GTPase_C, and E. coli polB/COG0417 with
EC 2.7.7.7 and ko:K02336.

This is v3's annotation logic over v5-derived data, not equivalent to
eggnog-mapper 2.x on the same DB; v3 filters donors by ev_lca ceiling and
sp_overlap, which v5 does not store authoritatively. Documented in USAGE.md.

=== 0c4882a feat(foldseek): selectable ModernProst checkpoint; fixes for large query sets

Preparation for running -m foldseek over a 404k-protein query set.

--modernprost_model selects the checkpoint used to predict 3Di and the
12-state alphabet (default gbouras13/modernprost-50M-pssm). Both alphabets
are model-specific, so the target DB and the queries searched against it
must use the same checkpoint; the help text says so.

Stop retaining the (L, 20) per-position distribution unless --profiles will
actually consume it. It was held for every query while only the PSSM path
reads it: 6.2 GB for an 83.7M-residue input. Measured peak RSS is now
1.41 GB for a 3k-protein slice of that set.

Strip trailing stop codons via a new clean_aa_sequence(), applied both to
the ModernProst input and to the amino-acid database in create_fs_db, which
is what keeps the AA, 3Di and 12-state strings the same length for a query.
'*' has no token, so terminal stops were becoming <unk> - an
out-of-distribution token producing a junk state at the C-terminus of 39% of
the queries at hand (157,771 of 404,085 sequences end in '*'; none have
internal stops). An internal '*' becomes X, preserving the residue count.

Throughput on the GB10 with the 50M checkpoint: 118 seq/s, ~24k residues/s,
i.e. ~57 min for the full 404k set.

Also ignore eggnongdb/, the local eggNOG download directory.

=== 5931ab2 perf(v5->v7): set-based LCA and bounded memory for a full-size v5 database

Sized against the real emapperdb-5.0.2: 23.7M proteins, 4.4M OGs and 75.4M
events (38 GB), versus 19k/27/504 in the test fixture.

Two things did not scale:

- event_index built a `kept` set of every surviving event id, i.e. a 75M
  element Python set (~4 GB). It now records only the rejects, which on a
  complete v5 DB is near-empty since every member name is in prots.

- ev_lca walked ordered lineage tracks pairwise per event. Sampling across
  the id range gives ~8 members and ~8 species per event, so that walk would
  have dominated the entire conversion. Replaced with an ancestor-set
  intersection plus a depth lookup, which runs in C, and memoised on the
  species set. Verified to produce byte-identical ev_lca values to the
  pairwise version on the fixture (504/504 events).

=== 77bf67d feat(foldseek): 12-state channel for PSSM profile queries

--profiles no longer forces --ss_12st 0. Foldseek supports the 12-state
alphabet for profile queries in a different on-disk form than for discrete
ones: instead of packing it into the _ss byte, it reads a sibling
<querydb>_ss12 database, and accepts that being a DBTYPE_HMM_PROFILE
(structurealign.cpp: queryHas12St = query3Di12St || (q12StDbr != NULL),
query12StProfileLayout). This writes that database from the model's 12-state
head.

- computeLogPSSM takes a background-frequency vector; BACKPROBS_12ST holds
  the 12-state background from Foldseek's data/mat12st.out.
- toBuffer_pssm_states packs an n-state PSSM into MMseqs' fixed 25-byte
  records (PROFILE_AA_SIZE 20 + 5), padding the unused score slots with -128
  so they can never be selected. Verified byte-identical to toBuffer_pssm for
  the 20-state 3Di case.
- Foldseek indexes a profile-layout 12-state matrix by amino-acid slot
  (subMatAA.aa2num[rowLetter]), not by 12-state index. No remapping is needed
  because mat12st.out and the AA matrix share the same letter order, so the
  12 states A C D E F G H I K L M N are AA slots 0..11.
- The 12-state distribution is only softmaxed and retained when --profiles
  needs it, so the discrete path keeps its bounded memory.

Verified against the real binary. With the _ss12 profile DB present,
--ss-12st 1 raises self-hit bitscores well above 3Di-only (e.g. 1139 -> 1633,
1178 -> 1681). Negative control: with _ss12 removed, --ss-12st 1 reproduces
the 3Di-only scores exactly, so the gain is attributable to this database and
not to some other flag effect.

=== eead171 fix(foldseek): match E-value calibration to 12-state scoring

Foldseek defaults to --evalue-nn-mode 0, the 3Di-only whole-query composition
network. Every search so far scored *with* the 12-state channel enabled while
calibrating E-values *without* it, which inflates significance badly. Mode 2 is
the 3Di+12-state network and requires a 12-state query, which --ss_12st
already guarantees, so it is now selected automatically whenever --ss_12st is
on. --evalue_nn_mode overrides.

Measured on 203 profile queries vs the 100k 12-state target DB: bitscores are
identical between modes (202/202, the network only affects calibration), while
E-values move by a median factor of 1.4e5 - median 2.51e-16 -> 2.98e-12, and
the fraction passing e<1e-3 drops from 100% to 94%.

Also exposed:
- --evalue_12st_profile_comp, Foldseek's --evalue-12st-profile-comp, which
  chooses where the mode-2 network takes the query composition from for
  profile queries (0 center/query sequence, 1 recover from profile scores).
- --use_reverse_score, default 1 matching Foldseek's own default, now emitted
  explicitly so the command line records it instead of relying on the build.

This is calibration only. It does not address the separate score-magnitude
problem: the 12-state PSSM is emitted on the 3Di bit-scale, giving the aligner
~9.2 per confident position against mat12st.out's diagonal of 1.9-4.3
(median 2.6). Bitscores are untouched by the NN mode, so that remains open.

=== 8805e98 fix(gitignore): stop "*old*" silently ignoring every foldseek-named path

".gitignore" carries "*old*", which matches "f-old-seek". An earlier commit
negated it only for eggnogmapper/search/foldseek/, so every *other*
foldseek-named file added since was silently dropped by "git add". Commit
ab4664a is the visible casualty: its message says it adds
environment-foldseek.yml, but the commit contains only the USAGE.md change
because the YAML was ignored.

Replaced with a general "!*foldseek*" negation placed after "*old*".
Verified that foo_old.py and bar.old.txt are still ignored.

Adds the files that had been dropped or were pending:
  environment-foldseek.yml          (should have landed in ab4664a)
  HANDOVER-foldseek-12state.md      handover for a collaborator
  scripts/build-foldseek-db.py      build a 12-state Foldseek target DB
  scripts/example-foldseek-runs.sh  the three-configuration comparison driver

=== 86ba841 chore(gitignore): keep HF model caches out of tracking

The new !*foldseek* negation also un-ignored tests/fixtures/foldseek/, which is
a 201 MB Hugging Face model cache created by running with --data_dir
tests/fixtures. Exclude it, and any models--* cache dir, explicitly.

